    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I do this all the time, I find that it makes it easier to read and understand the type if the bulk of the implementation is outside. That said I'm not sure <code>apply = apply</code> will work, I would use two different names, e.g., <code>apply = apply_helper</code> or something. I'm not aware of any conventions for the name, but I've seen \"help\" and \"helper\" used a few times by others, so that's what I'm using too.</p>",
        "id": 621178713,
        "sender_full_name": "Aurélien Geron",
        "timestamp": 1788389114
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried to give it a name like <code>apply = apply_impl</code></p>\n<p>Got the same error, it is maybe a weird edge case or so, idk. It works, with the changed Util.roc so I will go with that.</p>",
